    "turn_text": "what conservatives have primarily been asking for is something to legalize affordable health care plans. What a concept that... Right. Think about it. Obamacare made it illegal to have insurance companies offer and for individuals to purchase affordable health care plans. So we've been looking for something to do that. Now, the Senate bill makes insurance somewhat more affordable. They change actuarial value, they revise the age ban part of community rating. Again, these things start getting pretty technical, but according to CBO score, two years out, according to CBO, the Senate bill would produce premiums that are about 30% below the current Obamacare baseline. Now, I wish for a whole lot lower, and I think it could be if we really had the courage to address pre-existing conditions and other high-cost conditions in a very honest and forthright manner. You can cover people pre-existing conditions without collapsing insurance markets, which was the architecture of Obamacare, but because it's such a lightning rod issue, because it's politically risky to even talk about it, much less do something about it. That's been kind of my biggest disappointment we haven't then courageous enough to really",
